// The BREAK GATE must price a tab bar's fret-digit spacing floors exactly as the
// layout applies them (MultiStaffLayouter.ApplySharedColumnReservations — one list,
// two consumers). Before the list was shared, the gate priced these six bars of
// straight eighths WITHOUT the floors (SpacingRules.ApplyTabChordSpacing), packed
// all six onto ONE system, and the drawn digits ran to x=125.03 on a 119.50 page —
// the sixth bar clipped at the right edge (起票 2026-08-05,
// scratch/ベースタブLy/longtab.lys, reproduced verbatim here). Two systems of three
// bars is the claim; every element inside the page is the point.
// ⚠️ LilyPond sets the SAME six bars on one line (lysc-ly twin on 2.26.0: one
// system, every glyph on one Y row, width 119.5016) — and that is NOT
// counter-evidence: LP's tab digits are tiny where Lily#'s are a ratified ~2x
// enlargement (TabConstants.FretFontSize), so the digit floors that force the
// earlier break are that deviation's documented cost, not an un-ported quantity.
part melody {
  instrument bass
  section A {
    a8 a a a a a a a | a a a a a a a a | a a a a a a a a | a a a a a a a a | a a a a a a a a | a a a a a a a a |
  }
}

form main { A }

score main {
  tab melody
}
